From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sargun Vohra <sargunv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:41:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Carry OpenGL uniform blocks of a page and larger

Fixes two OpenGL crashes at the 8 KiB page of the uniform buffer
allocator. A block larger than a page owns its GL buffer and keeps no
CPU copy, but its update compared the new bytes against the empty
managed copy and crashed on the first change; it now uploads without
comparing. A block of exactly one page was rounded up past the page
size, so its first allocation failed and crashed; exact multiples of the
alignment now keep their size. Includes a plugin rendering regression.
Not yet proposed upstream.

Carried by maplibre-plugins until it lands upstream.
