+`0027-opengl-large-uniform-blocks.patch` fixes two OpenGL crashes for uniform
+blocks at and above the 8 KiB page of the uniform buffer allocator. A block
+larger than a page gets a GL buffer of its own and keeps no CPU copy, but its
+update compared the new bytes against the empty managed copy and crashed on the
+first change; it now uploads without comparing. A block of exactly one page
+rounded up past the page size, so its first allocation failed and crashed; the
+allocator now rounds exact multiples of the alignment to themselves. The patch
+includes a plugin rendering regression that reads back fragment-indexed layer
+blocks of 8176, 8192, 8208, and 16384 bytes across content changes. This patch
+is not yet proposed upstream.
+
 Each patch is the squashed diff of its upstream branch, applied on top of the
 patches before it, so a patch that adds a test next to an earlier patch's test
 carries that placement rather than the branch's own context.
